[AIMessage → tool] create_analysis({'text': 'Provenance conflict handling plan: 
Sources variably attribute the Ring of Nestor to Chamber Tomb 58 at Mycenae, a 
sepulchral treasure from Thisb\x12 in Boeotia, Nestor\x19s tomb at Pylos, or a 
ring purchased on the market by Arthur Evans. The evidence base does not allow 
these claims to be reconciled into a single secure archaeological context. For 
the article, the most neutral approach is to avoid asserting any one findspot as
fact. Instead, the provenance section should: (1) describe the ring as lacking a
secure excavation context; (2) summarize the different reported provenances with
precise attribution to the scholars or publications that advance them; (3) note 
that Evans is generally said to have acquired the ring rather than excavating it
in situ, which limits what can be stated about its original context; and (4) 
explain that this uncertainty has contributed to later doubts about the 
ring\x19s authenticity and its use as an example in discussions of Aegean 
forgeries. This treatment keeps the conflict transparent without privileging one
contested claim over others.', 'query_id': '20260628004741961396_57a34c8a'})
