"paper", "quality_score": 7, "access_score": 0}, {"source_id": 
"20260628004021325769_87368900", "title": "Knossos and the Prophets of 
Modernism", "url": 
"https://ndl.ethernet.edu.et/bitstream/123456789/42873/1/12..Cathy%20Gere.pdf", 
"source_type": "paper", "quality_score": 5, "access_score": 0}]}, {"id": 
"20260628004022148494_41cb3652", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The article notes 
that 'because of lingering skepticism, neither it nor the ring of Nestor ...' is
fully accepted, despite being considered an authentic work by some scholars.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628004021222852_03fa4b94"], "all_source_ids": 
["20260628004021222852_03fa4b94"], "citations": [7], "source_profiles": 
[{"source_id": "20260628004021222852_03fa4b94", "title": "Deconstructing a 
Narrative of Epiphany on the Isopata Ring", "url": 
"https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/pdfplus/10.2307/507325", "source_type": 
"paper", "quality_score": 9, "access_score": 0}]}, {"id": 
"20260628004105076589_586a3640", "type": "Claim", "text": "The \"Ring of 
Nestor\" is widely reported as a gold ring acquired by Arthur Evans, apparently 
originating from a tholos tomb at Kakovatos near or within the broader Mycenaean
sphere, though this provenance is qualified and not firmly established.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628004021247324_ba69cb65", 
"20260628004021300624_ad4df5cc"], "all_source_ids": 
["20260628004021247324_ba69cb65", "20260628004021300624_ad4df5cc"], "citations":
[8, 10], "source_profiles": [{"source_id": "20260628004021247324_ba69cb65", 
"title": "AN ANALYSIS OF LATE BRONZE AGE AEGEAN GLYPTIC MOTIFS OF A RELIGIOUS 
NATURE", "url": "https://etheses.bham.ac.uk/5467/1/Palmer14PhD.pdf", 
"source_type": "paper", "quality_score": 7, "access_score": 0}, {"source_id": 
"20260628004021300624_ad4df5cc", "title": "The Bronze Age Civilization of Greece
(Chapter 1 of Mycenaean Civilization)", "url": 
"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/mycenaean-civilization/bronze-age-civiliza
tion-of-greece/B0182E1380FB4B64662C85160A655AF7/core-reader", "source_type": 
"paper", "quality_score": 7, "access_score": 0}]}, {"id": 
"20260628004105269246_caf4cd01", "type": "Claim", "text": "In treatments of 
Minoan–Mycenaean religion and Aegean glyptic, the \"Ring of Nestor\" is cited as
a significant artefact whose imagery includes a composite creature described as 
a Minoan dragon standing on grassy ground before a tree.", "source_ids": 
["20260628004021277210_78e5b375"], "all_source_ids": 
["20260628004021277210_78e5b375", "20260628004021354207_3f325615"], "citations":
[9], "source_profiles": [{"source_id": "20260628004021277210_78e5b375", "title":
"Composite creatures on seals and sealings: fixed hybrids and more", "url": 
"https://books.ub.uni-heidelberg.de/propylaeum/catalog/view/502/762/85410", 
"source_type": "paper", "quality_score": 7, "access_score": 0}, {"source_id": 
"20260628004021354207_3f325615", "title": "Minoan-Mycenaean Religion and its 
Survival in Greek Religion", "url": 
"https://eclass.uoa.gr/modules/document/file.php/ARCH375/Nilsson-The%20Minoan-My
cenaean%20religion%20and%20its%20survival%20in%20Greek%20religion-C.%20W.%20K.%2
0Gleerup%20%281927%29.pdf", "source_type": "paper", "quality_score": 5, 
"access_score": 0}]}, {"id": "20260628004022286389_3e815f09", "type": 
"Evidence", "text": "The composite-creatures study remarks: 'On the Ring of 
Nestor, a Minoan Dragon can also be seen in a natural setting. It is standing on
a grassy ground in front of the trunk of the tree whose branches ...'.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628004021277210_78e5b375"], "all_source_ids": 
["20260628004021277210_78e5b375"], "citations": [9], "source_profiles": 
[{"source_id": "20260628004021277210_78e5b375", "title": "Composite creatures on
seals and sealings: fixed hybrids and more", "url": 
"https://books.ub.uni-heidelberg.de/propylaeum/catalog/view/502/762/85410", 
"source_type": "paper", "quality_score": 7, "access_score": 0}]}, {"id": 
"20260628004105340573_aa457d4a", "type": "Claim", "text": "One line of scholarly
argument holds that, given the \"Ring of Nestor\"’s alleged provenance in 
Mycenae or the Kakovatos tholos, its imagery should not be interpreted as 
depicting Neopalatial Cretan rituals.", "source_ids": 
["20260628004021247324_ba69cb65"], "all_source_ids": 
["20260628004021247324_ba69cb65"], "citations": [8], "source_profiles": 
[{"source_id": "20260628004021247324_ba69cb65", "title": "AN ANALYSIS OF LATE 
BRONZE AGE AEGEAN GLYPTIC MOTIFS OF A RELIGIOUS NATURE", "url": 
"https://etheses.bham.ac.uk/5467/1/Palmer14PhD.pdf", "source_type": "paper", 
"quality_score": 7, "access_score": 0}]}, {"id": 
"20260628004022218804_0e90ded9", "type": "Evidence", "text": "In Palmer’s thesis
the discussion of the ring of Nestor states that 'this, coupled with the ring’s 
alleged provenance in Mycenae, suggests that the ring does not refer to 
Neopalatial rituals'.", "source_ids": ["20260628004021247324_ba69cb65"], 
"all_source_ids": ["20260628004021247324_ba69cb65"], "citations": [8], 
"source_profiles": [{"source_id": "20260628004021247324_ba69cb65", "title": "AN 
ANALYSIS OF LATE BRONZE AGE AEGEAN GLYPTIC MOTIFS OF A RELIGIOUS NATURE", "url":
"https://etheses.bham.ac.uk/5467/1/Palmer14PhD.pdf", "source_type": "paper", 
"quality_score": 7, "access_score": 0}]}, {"id": 
"20260628004022353798_2787c8e8", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The chapter on 
Bronze Age Greece observes: 'From the tholos tomb in Kakovatos – apparently – 
comes the famous ring that Evans acquired, the “ring of Nestor”, whose 
authenticity is disputed'.", "source_ids": ["20260628004021300624_ad4df5cc"], 
"all_source_ids": ["20260628004021300624_ad4df5cc"], "citations": [10], 
"source_profiles": [{"source_id": "20260628004021300624_ad4df5cc", "title": "The
Bronze Age Civilization of Greece (Chapter 1 of Mycenaean Civilization)", "url":
"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/mycenaean-civilization/bronze-age-civiliza
tion-of-greece/B0182E1380FB4B64662C85160A655AF7/core-reader", "source_type": 
"paper", "quality_score": 7, "access_score": 0}]}, {"id": 
"20260628004022477535_b85eb645", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Nilsson states 
