"20260628004107903013_da5ccfd2", "type": "Claim", "text": "The shifting 
scholarly assessments of the Ring of Nestor—from early acceptance, through 
classifications as a suspect object and arguments against authenticity, to later
defenses of its genuineness—have been used to illustrate that archaeological 
interpretations of artifacts are historically contingent and shaped by changing 
scholarly positions and social dynamics, not solely by material evidence.", 
